 /* Where YUView puts the data it derives from a source file and can recreate at any time: decoded YUV
  * and per-block analysis statistics.
  *
- * The requested location is ".YUViewBD" next to the executable, so a portable install keeps its
- * cache with it. That directory is not writable in every deployment (an AppImage mount, a read-only
- * install prefix), so the first call probes it once and falls back to the user cache directory. The
- * fallback can be overridden with the setting "BDCache/directory".
+ * The location is ".bd_analyzer" in the working directory - where the analyzer was started, not
+ * where its binary lives. Decoded YUV runs to gigabytes, so it has to land on a volume the user
+ * picked; an RPM install puts the binary under a root-owned /opt, and anything derived from that
+ * path ends up somewhere small and unexpected. Start the analyzer from the volume with the room.
  *
- * Everything under the root is disposable. The user is asked on exit whether to delete it.
+ * The setting "BDCache/directory" overrides it with a fixed path. There is no other fallback: a
+ * working directory that cannot be written to means no caching, and every caller already handles
+ * an empty root that way.
+ *
+ * Everything under the root is disposable, and MainWindow::closeEvent deletes it on exit without
+ * asking - it can all be recreated from the source files.
  */
